<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Wagang Army</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">611–<a href="/years/618">618</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Wagang Army was one of the largest rebel forces in the collapse of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sui-dynasty">Sui dynasty</a>, named after its base at Wagang in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henan">Henan</a>. Founded by Zhai Rang around 611 and led from 617 by Li Mi, it seized the granaries near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luoyang">Luoyang</a> and dominated the central plain, but was crushed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wang-shichong">Wang Shichong</a> in 618, and many of its leaders went over to the Tang.</p></div>
